Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight Private Permit Bridge P0 Dual Hemisphere Review

@ [dual_review_uuid] b72cb6c6-92cb-4752-9143-628d03cb90c5
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 750fbbb5-f72f-4816-882f-d8b0ebf1acc7

& [ConstructiveHemisphere]
  + use Rust ownership as the capability ledger: opaque admission moves into issuance permit moves into the runner and only a terminal outcome returns
  + retain the published runner process and receipt logic unchanged while adding the smallest internal join needed by a later authorized initiator
  + verify successful runner truth by canonical round-trip and existing receipt validator before terminal classification

& [AdversarialHemisphere]
  + treat pub exports constructors serde cloning defaults persistence retry loops and callback reuse as capability multiplication
  + treat a correspondence-verified signed form as insufficient because the published pure implementation explicitly leaves identity custody trusted time and consent external
  + treat every runner error after issuance as an uncertain spent physical attempt even if no process receipt was returned
  + treat provider-unavailable as a terminal observed result rather than permission for model download service repair or fallback

& [Synthesis]
  + a crate-private affine move chain with pre-mint validation a FnOnce internal seam and terminal post-consumption projection is the smallest defensible bridge
  + structural unreachability is preserved until later live initiation adds the only production admission constructor inside a separately governed nested module
